**Rule (Publication codec)** · `rule:publication:codec` The host encodes and decodes epoch's constructible disclosures under the test publication namespace reserved by (`[ROOT-amend:design:test-publication-profile]`). The complete field theory lives beside the implementation and is assigned by interchange's validating registry producer at the declared test coordinate. Its identity uses interchange's existing normalized-theory recipe under (`[ROOT-req:identity:admission-record]`); exhaustive field destructuring and closed variant matches make a carrier extension a compile-time obligation. No separate digest or hash vocabulary is introduced. Records are fixed-length arrays with named positions in that theory; variants carry explicit integer tags. Missing, extra, duplicate, unsupported and noncanonical values refuse. The canonical identity is the full document bytes: this theory admits exactly version 1.0.0, and any nonzero patch refuses separately from an unsupported namespace, major or minor. A later patch needs a declared theory version; it is never an alternate spelling of this disclosure. Mathematical rationals use reduced numerator and positive-denominator decimal-text pairs. Where a replay assertion retains a numerical source spelling, that spelling accompanies its reduced value and must agree with it; authored coordinate integer pairs remain separate integers without reduction. Platform-sized indices have an unsigned 64-bit wire range and a checked conversion on the receiving platform. Frames and act sequences retain their order; cause collections and mathematical sets use canonical structural order. All arithmetic limits are caller inputs, and resource refusal is not admission.

**Rule (Publication authority)** · `rule:publication:authority` Decoding yields only untrusted disclosures. Epoch's restore function constructs checked values, compares the sections and replays the package, including every restored ridge charge under its admitted verifier. Neither a digest nor a decoded flag substitutes for this consumption. Authentication fields are retained byte for byte; their cryptographic meaning remains (`[ROOT-open:crypto:dependency-admission]`). The host-side fixture verifier attests only its declared synthetic causes and policies.

